 "predeclared_rule": "Hit-count prediction: one source (trunk T + long tail, checkpoint_at=[T]) holds the junction T and the two near-end checkpoints N-4-ub and N-4. For each c in {T, N-4-ub, N-4} and delta in {-1, 0, +1} a child shares exactly c+delta tokens with the source and then diverges (distinct next token). One launch per drafter configuration (as given, no drafter, others given). SATISFIED for a configuration iff every cell n_fork_tokens == the KPF-11 prediction and no cell has n_fork_tokens == 0 while the prediction is > 0 (an unidentified drafter configuration must not disable fork reuse). A drafter-dependent drop is MEASURED once, at a held-out shared length that is not any c-1/c/c+1: drop = predicted - observed there, plus a cold-run first-token comparison at that length; the drop is recorded, never subtracted from the main cells.",
 "predeclared_rules_sha256": "049d663e7a57cbd70b56bb5bd1e8d1551aedcca3275dc728c8e57af90889b8c9",
